Q1. What is Docker Compose, and why do we use it?

Interview Ready Answer

Docker Compose is a tool used to define and manage multi-container Docker
applications. It allows all services, networks, volumes, and
configurations to be defined in a single docker-compose.yml file, so the
entire application stack can be started and managed using a single
command.

Definition

Docker Compose
- Tool for multi-container Docker applications.
- Uses a YAML configuration file.
- Manages multiple containers together.

Purpose

• Start multiple containers together.
• Simplify application deployment.
• Reduce multiple docker run commands.
• Maintain consistent configuration.

======================================================================

Q2. What are the benefits of Docker Compose?

Interview Ready Answer

Docker Compose simplifies the management of multi-container
applications. It allows all services, networks, volumes, and
configurations to be defined in a single docker-compose.yml file,
reducing manual effort and ensuring consistent deployment.

Benefits

• Single configuration file.
• Start entire application using one command.
• Easier management of multiple containers.
• Automatic network creation.
• Better consistency across environments.
• Reduced manual configuration.

======================================================================

Q3. What is a docker-compose.yml file?

Interview Ready Answer

The docker-compose.yml file is a YAML configuration file used to define
a multi-container Docker application. It specifies services, Docker
images, port mappings, networks, volumes, environment variables, and
other configuration required to run the application.

Definition

docker-compose.yml
- YAML configuration file.
- Read by Docker Compose.
- Defines the complete application stack.

Purpose

• Define services.
• Configure ports.
• Configure volumes.
• Configure networks.
• Configure environment variables.

