Q4. Name two commonly used Docker Compose commands.

Interview Ready Answer

docker compose up

Starts and creates all services defined in the docker-compose.yml file.
It also creates required networks and volumes if they do not already
exist.

------------------------------------------------------------

docker compose down

Stops and removes all containers, networks, and other resources created
by Docker Compose.

Other Common Commands

docker compose start
→ Starts existing containers.

docker compose stop
→ Stops running containers.

docker compose ps
→ Lists Compose-managed containers.

docker compose logs
→ Displays logs of running containers.

